  "body": "Source: the research of #2395 and the maintainer's decision of 2026-11-17 (question dialog): \"Router machine kind (Recommended)\".\n\n**Decision**\n- CamCraft gets no Router tab.\n- A machine of kind Router shows the Nest node and the router options on the Milling tab. It hides the operations and options that do not apply to a router.\n\n**Why**\n- The router functions are jobs at sheet level (nesting, grain, labels, remnants) and options on operations that exist (tabs, corner relief, drill blocks). They are not one operation family.\n- Nesting has its own tree node in #2163.\n\n**Scope**\n1. The machine file states the kind Router where it does not do so now. The check starts with the router machines of #1915 and #1918.\n2. One function decides which operations, pages and options a machine kind shows. The UI and MCP read the same function.\n3. A hidden operation that is already in a project stays visible and is not deleted.\n4. The router sub-issues attach their options to this function: #2398, #2399, #2400, #2401, #2402, #2404, #2405, #2406, #2407, #2408, #2409.\n\nDone means:\n- A project with a router machine shows the router options on the Milling tab.\n- A project with a mill shows no router option.\n- A test asserts the two lists, in the UI layer and through MCP.\n",
